# Bluesky document-plane CURVE certificates, generated by `osprey deploy up`.
# The *.key_secret files are private keys, and the public halves are bearer
# material too (holding the manager's public key is enough to reach its
# control socket), so the whole directory stays out of version control —
# same treatment as .env above.
#
# Leading slash on purpose: this anchors the pattern to the project root, so
# it matches only the directory `osprey deploy up` writes. An unanchored
# `bluesky_curve/` would match a directory of that name ANYWHERE in the tree,
# and git would then silently skip such a path on `git add` — the failure mode
# is a file that looks committed but never was.
/data/bluesky_curve/

